# Test: a dashboard count leads to exactly the rows it counts
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-ui-1 user story 1 -- the operator opens the estate,
#            follows the count of devices in a failing state on the Devices
#            card, and lands on the devices table filtered to those devices
# PREVENTS: a card count whose link opens a table that lists other rows, or
#           a different number of rows than the card said
#
# Goal: prove the path from the estate dashboard to the failing devices in a
# browser.
# Method: the Devices card draws one legend link per display state, the word
# and its count (handler_dashboard_cards.go devicesCardView, linking
# state:<key>). The sample estate has exactly one device in the Down state,
# edge-ams-02, whose BGP component is down (sample/estate.go; Down 1 in
# TestSampleEstateInvariants). The script never changes a health component
# (sample/script.go scriptSteps), so its timer cannot move that count. The
# test clicks "Down 1", then reads the address and the content region: one
# match of 44, the row of edge-ams-02, and no row of a healthy device.
# TestDashboardLinkCountsEqualTargetRows proves every count equals its rows in
# process; this proves a browser follows the link to them.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_fleet_ui_sample:state=present
option=timeout:value=60s
option=viewport:width=1600:height=1000

action=open:path=/fleet/
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=Down
action=click:text=Down 1
expect=url:contains=/fleet/estate/devices/
expect=url:contains=q=state%3Adown
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=1 of 44 devices
expect=html:id=fleet-content:contains=edge-ams-02
expect=html:id=fleet-content:not-contains=edge-ams-01
